**There are still blockers. I would not start the paid draws yet.** For example, the planned split preflight can say a rebuilt handover matches even when its source date differs, because it does not compare that field. The design currently describes this as a complete handover comparison.

The review below is read-only. I did not run the split preflight: the probe log showed only the first day completed when I checked.

### Round-1 findings

1. **Partly resolved — test articles.** [bench_test_articles.py:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_test_articles.py:63) selects the frozen test articles; I verified that all 30 distinct IDs exist in the item database. But [benchmark-design.md:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:96) makes their results reporting only, while [line 112](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:112) permits a broad positive verdict regardless of a test-set regression. The test results must be able to qualify or prevent that verdict.

2. **Partly resolved — chance of rejecting the same configuration.** I independently scored all six stored draws and reproduced the listed values and the arithmetic at [benchmark-design.md:68](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:68): helpful counts **169, 161, 179, 161, 167, 169**; core **78, 77, 78, 73, 76, 75**; judgement agreements **15, 15, 16, 15, 16, 14**. Across the 20 ordered partitions, the three individual limits fail **1, 0 and 0** times respectively; the combined numerical limits fail once. These partitions reuse six draws and are not 20 independent experiments. More importantly, passing a limit that permits losses does not establish “at least as good”; the verdict needs to describe the observed differences and margins instead.

3. **Partly resolved — extraction versus written records.** [bench_measure.py:80](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_measure.py:80) now scores both the checked handover and written evidence. But [line 98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_measure.py:98) reports only broad endpoints, not the specific check or later action responsible for a loss. The reading procedure still needs the stored drops and trace to explain each miss.

4. **Resolved — question counting aid.** [bench_measure.py:74](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_measure.py:74) calls the existing `score_ref.same_question`; [benchmark-design.md:106](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:106) identifies its limitation and makes the blind read, rather than its count, decisive.

5. **Partly resolved — comparability gate.** The fixture hash matches the stated value, and the comparator now checks the added tables. I reran it: it still exits **1** for four `revisions.said_day` differences, as [benchmark-design.md:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:57) discloses. The documented explanation is credible, but [plan-final.md:78](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-final.md:78) requires reproduction of the stored ledger; the exception has not been resolved against that requirement. Also, the comparator omits `dependency_resolutions` and `thesis_group_aliases`; I checked that both happen to be empty in this particular pair, but “every table” is too broad.

6. **Resolved — refused-answer replay claim.** [bench_run.py:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_run.py:45) now confines the claim to this archive and explicitly disclaims general ordering.

7. **Partly resolved — reading packet.** [bench_measure.py:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_measure.py:167) writes a per-matter, per-draw matrix for window draws. It does not create one for test draws, include source and answer references, or give loss reasons. The procedure at [benchmark-design.md:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:98) still reads only misses with a particular 2-of-3 comparison, rather than every missed helpful entry required by §7.2.

8. **Partly resolved — disclosures and pins.** [bench_measure.py:133](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_measure.py:133) prints the standard version, page hash, gold hash and D373 concern. However, the design hash file claimed at [benchmark-design.md:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:47) does not exist. The test manifest also does not hash its own harness or the measurement script, and its resume behavior can overwrite the original manifest.

9. **Partly resolved — pre-draw checks and attribution.** [benchmark-design.md:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:16) correctly names the three architectural differences and avoids attributing the result solely to extraction. The preflight remains pending, and its proposed use has the substantive gaps below.

### Remaining blockers and serious findings

1. **Blocker — the split preflight does not prove what the design claims.** [preflight_split.py:34](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/preflight_split.py:34) compares the archive’s sorted-key request identity, not the bytes sent over the wire. Production serializes the request in its original key order at [model.py:125](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/model.py:125); the identity sorts keys at [model.py:206](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/model.py:206). Also, [preflight_split.py:41](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/preflight_split.py:41) compares selected fields only: it omits, among other things, evidence `original_day`, candidate object and rung contents, drops and groups. It iterates only stored handovers and can skip missing inputs without failing at [lines 63–70](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/preflight_split.py:63). Calling production code does not by itself establish that a reconstructed request has the same wire bytes.

   **Fix:** after the probe completes, compare production-serialized requests, compare the complete behavior-relevant handover and drops, reconcile the handovers against the dispatched population, and report every skipped or refused case. Check that altered source, snapshot, answer and an omitted handover are detected. Run the applicable stored-data checks for matching records as well; the replay gate alone does not perform the checks described in §5.

2. **Blocker — the declared verdict can conceal a real regression.** [benchmark-design.md:111](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:111) allows “at least as good” with up to eight fewer helpful matters on average, up to three fewer core matters, and three fewer judgement agreements; test results cannot independently stop it. The small control sample estimates how often these limits would reject those six historical draws, not equivalence or an acceptable loss. **Fix:** predeclare a conclusion that reports the actual differences, uncertainty and test results; settle the acceptance limits and the D203 gate exception under the authority required by [plan-final.md:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-final.md:96) before launch.

3. **Serious — a restarted test draw can mix versions and misstate its identity.** [bench_test_articles.py:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_test_articles.py:59) reuses existing handovers and archive, then [line 69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_test_articles.py:69) overwrites the manifest with current hashes without checking the earlier ones. A resumed draw could therefore combine answers made under different code or inputs while claiming one version. [bench_run.py:153](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/bench_run.py:153) likewise accepts an existing ledger without verifying its origin. **Fix:** preserve the original manifest, verify all relevant hashes and the draw identity before resuming, and refuse mismatches; use fresh draw folders for fresh draws.

4. **Serious — the reading plan can miss errors shared by both arms.** At [benchmark-design.md:99](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:99), a helpful fact missed by both arms, or missed once rather than twice, need not be read. The matter matcher is explicitly a counting aid, not a semantic judge ([score_gold.py:58](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/score_gold.py:58)). **Fix:** produce a traceable packet for **every missed helpful entry in each draw**, including test draws, with the source, raw answers, checked handover, drops and written records; independently read the required samples of hits and extras.

5. **Serious — the proposed freeze is not yet in place.** There is no `benchmark-design.sha256` beside the design despite [benchmark-design.md:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/benchmark-design.md:48). The current page hash I measured is `9f4da61cce4057ee9a0f001d671662a859ac0a4d552ada072332a6eb3fbf040e`; that observation is not a pre-launch freeze. **Fix:** after the remaining design and harness issues are resolved, record and verify the final design, both harnesses, measurement code, configuration, inputs and fixture before the first draw.

The split preflight is a useful starting check, but **its current design and implementation are not a sound launch gate**. Its result must remain pending until the probe completes, and a pass on its present selected fields would not close the gaps above.

